WEBVTT

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.130
Crap...

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.260
We're out of everything else, so now we're out of time?

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.370
Brother!

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.180
What?!

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.330
That little twerp!

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.270
He's stealing our thunder!

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:27.480
Is he all right now?

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.520
Don't worry about Garrod.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.550
Brother, the GX, it-

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.080
I don't believe it... It's been upgraded?

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.750
Let's do this!

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:55.880
<b>After War</b>

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:55.880
<b>GUNDAM</b>

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:03.380
<b>The dream I'd nearly forgotten is beginning to stir,</b>

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:06.340
<b>little by little</b>

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:10.890
<b>filling in the gaps in my heart</b>

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:18.290
<b>The instant my frozen memories begin to awaken,</b>

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:27.820
<b>my only wish is for the future that is about to begin</b>

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.420
<b>I'll reach out with both hands</b>

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.090
<b>and embrace that dream I once had</b>

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.000
<b>I want to go on believing</b>

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.760
<b>without ever letting go or giving up</b>

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.310
<b>Until the day comes when I grab hold...</b>

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:50.230
<b>...of that dream I once had,</b>

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:53.750
<b>I want to keep chasing after it</b>

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:59.780
<b>without ever forgetting my hopes and dreams</b>

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.960
<b>Episode 12</b>

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:09.960
<b>"He Is My Masterpiece"</b>

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:11.580
Let's do this!

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.180
What's he doing?

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.180
That's totally his style.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.760
He's got too much enthusiasm.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.770
Can he do this without any practice?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:29.730
Keep watching.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:33.480
Here they come!

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.070
Use the Divider!

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:39.570
Like this?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.450
Pretty cool, huh?

00:02:58.550 --> 00:02:59.170
Brother!

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.680
Just what I was waiting for!

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.100
Brother!

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.770
Impossible...

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.980
Its offensive capabilities have been increased!

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:15.110
No, not just its performance.

00:03:16.070 --> 00:03:18.360
It's also Garrod's instincts.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:21.070
He has an extraordinary instinct for piloting mobile suits.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:25.660
With adaptability in particular, he's shown the instincts of a natural pilot.

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.870
With all his crazy enthusiasm, you'd never guess it, though.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.330
I hate sitting here and letting him steal our thunder!

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:35.460
That doesn't sit right with me!

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:38.170
We're done here.

00:03:38.170 --> 00:03:39.510
I can still fight.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.130
No, it's over.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:45.890
We didn't factor in the GX being upgraded.

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.220
It's too risky to continue fighting it.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.680
But, Brother!

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:53.770
Olba, don't let your emotions get the better of you.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.560
Remember what our true objective is.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:02.070
This isn't the proper place for us to lay down our lives.

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:04.700
Understood, Brother.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.160
Pursuing them would be pointless.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:14.330
Yeah.

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.050
Olba!

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:23.630
I don't want them to think we were beaten!

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.640
They're coming back?

00:04:29.890 --> 00:04:32.270
Use the Harmonica Cannon, Gundam Boy!

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:34.600
You mean this?

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.400
Oh, no! Olba!

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.240
Eat this!

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.620
Brother!

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.630
Olba...

00:05:02.710 --> 00:05:04.630
Don't say anything, Brother.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.760
Your pain is coming through to me...

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:21.730
Hey!

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:22.940
Where's he going?!

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.650
Don't tell me he's going to try to rescue Tiffa!

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:29.070
There he goes, running off half-cocked again!

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:41.380
It won't work. If I fought him now, I'd only lose again.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.920
I have to become stronger!

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.860
Cdr. Carris, is something the matter?

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.570
No. Everything is quiet?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:11.240
Yes, sir.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.470
Look at that...!

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.600
It's magnificent!

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:41.730
Fire!

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:53.820
Simulation complete. You were blown up.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:57.790
How about that? Pretty good, huh?

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:01.540
The pattern's completely random, but they move almost like the real thing!

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.000
They move better than in the simulators we used to use in the military.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.550
One more time! Give me another crack at it!

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.440
I'm sorry, Brother. This is my fault.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:33.410
You'll probably be angry with me, but I can't let them get away with this.

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:36.370
I'll destroy them myself!

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:51.630
Sorry I'm late!

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:54.340
Any luck? How did you make out?

00:07:55.970 --> 00:07:56.800
Panache.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:57.760
Right away.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:07:59.430
Great!

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:03.140
I have most of their defense force's emplacements and fighting strength.

00:08:03.640 --> 00:08:05.480
Then I guess it's time for us to slip out.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:09.940
Wow, that girl they rescued a while ago is being kept safe in the city?

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:13.400
It says here that those lousy Vultures really did a number on her!

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.870
I'm just glad she's safe now.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:16.820
That's for sure.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.530
Media manipulation.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:23.370
Which means we're the enemies of this town's fine citizens.

00:08:26.210 --> 00:08:27.630
That must be the place.

00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.300
That's all for today.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:43.520
Three days have passed since the team began Bit combat training simulations.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:48.690
However, as if mocking the hard work of Garrod and the others,

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:51.480
time simply passed by with nothing to show for it.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.700
Man, I'm beat!

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.700
I'm starting to get fed up.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.160
Quit your whining! Man up!

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:08.040
Hey, I'm the type of guy who hates hard work.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.380
Show some backbone, damn it.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:13.960
You gonna whine like him, Garrod?

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:19.850
I want power...

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:23.310
The power to fight a Newtype.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.020
The power to rescue Tiffa.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:29.520
I want power!

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:44.160
I see. So we're being made out to be vile Vultures who are hunting an innocent girl.

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:46.790
That's-

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:49.670
Hey!

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.800
There he goes again, another youthful meltdown.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:54.090
Wait!

00:09:54.710 --> 00:09:56.970
If you're going, take only the clothes on your back.

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.930
Why did you let him leave?

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.140
He's aware of his own limitations now.

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:12.110
Ah. He might try something unreasonable, but not something impossible.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.940
That's right.

00:10:14.020 --> 00:10:18.450
I'm skeptical. When you're 15, you're still half a child.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.280
Yes, but the other half is an adult.

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:31.330
A woman named Ennil El is here.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:34.170
She says that she has come here to see you, Mr. Mayor.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:37.630
Ennil? I don't know the name.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:38.970
About that...

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:43.760
She said that if I showed you this, you would want to see her, sir.

00:10:47.640 --> 00:10:49.520
Th-This is...

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.940
Bring her to me immediately.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:13.330
You're clear.

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:14.500
Okay, thanks.

00:11:25.010 --> 00:11:28.430
So, it looks like you've seen that picture.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:32.770
What are you after? Money? Or do you want-

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:50.830
Forgive me, I didn't show you that photo with the intention of blackmailing you.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.960
I know that voice! It couldn't be...

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.420
Why else would you show something like this to me?

00:11:57.840 --> 00:12:01.380
Or rather, how do you even have this picture?

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:07.850
Take a good look at my face.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.060
You can't be!

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:15.560
I knew it, it's Ennil El!

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:23.030
But I am. The man in the picture with you, Rear Admiral Narda El, is my father.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:25.570
Well, I never!

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:30.200
As for you, Mayor Nomoa... Or should I call you "Doctor"?

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.660
My father told me all about you when he was alive.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.120
Doctor?

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:38.290
Oh, so your father has passed away...

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:40.670
Yes, he's dead.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.170
Both my father and mother have died.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.340
I see...

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:52.770
During the war, your father did me an enormous favor.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:56.480
If there is anything I can do for you, don't hesitate to ask.

00:12:57.440 --> 00:12:59.520
There's just one thing.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:00.980
What is it?

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:05.400
I want the pilot of the GX-9900.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:08.570
Alive or dead, I don't particularly care.

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:10.280
Consider it done.

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.870
Thank you.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:16.370
To express my gratitude, I can offer you my assistance.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:18.380
With what?

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:22.630
Don't play innocent. Father used to tell stories.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:24.340
About all sorts of things.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:29.760
Then I'll show you. Follow me.

00:13:43.610 --> 00:13:47.610
What's the matter? Did you think I was your friend who snuck into the castle?

00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:52.280
Remember, I also have powers.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:06.010
This is the giant mobile armor Patulia,

00:14:06.130 --> 00:14:08.970
which can unleash terrible power when operated by a Newtype.

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:11.760
Our army's star of hope.

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:16.350
Operation Lilac. Right, Mayor Nomoa?

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:20.060
Down here, I think I'd rather be called by my true name.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:23.150
As you wish, Dr. Dorat.

00:14:26.900 --> 00:14:29.860
When he was alive, my father used to say something again and again.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.950
That if that operation had succeeded,

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:37.040
the war would have ended in victory for the Space Revolutionary Army.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.580
I believe so, as well.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:45.050
If only Operation Lilac had succeeded...

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:48.970
Operation Lilac.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:55.930
An Earth landing operation conducted by the S.R.A. prior to the colony drop.

00:14:57.140 --> 00:14:59.560
The S.R.A.'s decisive weapon was a Newtype squad...

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:02.770
...made up of the Patulia, a giant mobile armor designed for Newtypes,

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:07.070
as well as five Bertigos, which would go down to Earth.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:12.490
They would meet up with a sleeper cell that had mixed in with the populace...

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:16.950
...and then eliminate the U.N.E. in one blow.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.250
But the operation failed.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:23.330
The Newtype squad that was to be our trump card...

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.840
...was wiped out in a battle during reentry.

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:29.840
The Patulia itself was thrown wildly off course.

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:35.510
Your father, who had been sent here as a sleeper agent,

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:38.720
helped us make our escape.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:41.850
That was four months before the war ended.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:45.360
Did your father perish in the colony drop?

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:50.740
No, it happened after the war. He was murdered.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.360
Murdered?!

00:15:53.860 --> 00:15:59.540
When I was nine, Father was killed right in front of me.

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:05.080
Word got out to the Earthers that Father was an S.R.A. officer.

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:09.340
Since I was just a child and Mother was an Earth native,

00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:11.670
my life was spared, but barely.

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:17.220
But I'll never forget the frustration I felt when I was robbed of my father.

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.310
When he was alive, Father said something to me.

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:26.440
That even if the war ended, you would probably go on fighting.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:31.070
Of course. I preach peace to the citizenry...

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:35.570
...and I advocate for unifying the world and invoke it whenever I'm with Carris.

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:38.740
But my true goal...

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:41.370
...is the eradication of all humans on Earth.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.290
I'm with you.

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:49.420
Oh, I get it... That old man there and Miss Sexy are both from the colonies!

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:53.170
When do you plan to activate the Patulia?

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:56.890
It will probably be after I get a clearer picture of Tiffa's abilities.

00:16:57.590 --> 00:16:59.550
Frankly, I'm having trouble deciding.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.390
Tiffa or Carris? Which do I make the Petulia's pilot?

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:07.400
That Carris boy is one of your products, isn't he?

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.560
He is.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:11.320
He is my masterpiece.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:16.660
Of all I have made, he is the one with the most power and fewest disorders.

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:21.540
As an Artificial Newtype, it would be safe to call him a perfect specimen.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.040
Artificial Newtype?

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.000
Any unusual activity?

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:30.540
Nothing yet, sir.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:34.130
No way! Then that means that pilot isn't...

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:36.630
Who's there?!

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:37.630
Oh, crap!

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:39.850
The boy!

00:17:39.970 --> 00:17:41.010
You know him?

00:17:41.350 --> 00:17:42.930
That's the GX's pilot!

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:50.190
Captain! I'm seeing activity in Fort Severn!

00:17:50.560 --> 00:17:52.070
It must be Garrod.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:53.690
Send out Witz and Roabea!

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:54.440
Yes, sir!

00:17:54.690 --> 00:17:57.650
Heat source closing in fast! It's a mobile armor!

00:18:00.530 --> 00:18:03.040
I'm going to make you feel my brother's pain!

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:10.670
Come on, we need to go into town! He sure picked a lousy time to come!

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:15.380
Let's make quick work of him.

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.060
Let's begin!

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:42.910
Damn it!

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.000
I knew it was you.

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.120
You're...

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:51.210
You're that pilot from before!

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:52.420
That's right.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:54.210
Then you need to hear this!

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.380
You're going to beg for your life?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.260
You're being lied to!

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:01.050
That's certainly surprising.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:06.260
Hear me out. You think you have a Newtype's powers,

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:08.770
but they were created in a lab!

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:13.230
Your mayor is really a scientist who was in the S.R.A.!

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:19.070
He's the one who gave you your abilities! He wants Newtype powers!

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:25.700
And he's sacrificed countless lives to create you.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:28.620
That has to be news to you!

00:19:29.700 --> 00:19:33.670
You're being lied to! There's no reason for us to fight!

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:37.170
Come on, put down your gun and run away with us!

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:41.630
Oh, that? I've known for a long time.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:48.140
Yes, I was once an ordinary human.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:52.270
But I wanted power.

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:56.770
And so I asked Mayor Nomoa to turn me into an Artificial Newtype.

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.070
You did what?!

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:02.280
The old me was an ordinary, insignificant human.

00:20:02.780 --> 00:20:07.160
But I wanted to reform this world more than anything.

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:09.580
It requires power to do that.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.290
I needed superhuman power.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:16.960
A bunch of people were killed in the process of creating you!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:22.010
Don't you yourself fight to survive? Don't start spouting humanism now.

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:25.010
It's something that we've all experienced.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:29.850
The wish to acquire superhuman, absolute power.

00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.270
I simply followed through on it.

00:20:34.730 --> 00:20:39.230
Fortunately, research into producing Artificial Newtypes has made great strides.

00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:45.200
Subjects used to suffer from memory gaps, headaches, and mood swings,

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:47.620
but it's mostly trouble-free now.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:54.080
One day, a select few with pure hearts will gain Newtype-like powers, just as I have.

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.920
We can then found a millennial kingdom in a real sense on this world.

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:03.170
I am simply the advance guard of that grand plan.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.590
It's true, I wanted to get power.

00:21:07.090 --> 00:21:08.510
But I was wrong!

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:11.850
It's... I can't explain it, but that has to be wrong!

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:15.640
Then that means you must reject her, as well.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:19.860
I'm... different.

00:21:20.110 --> 00:21:23.820
I'm not like you!

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:26.700
Impossible!

00:21:26.780 --> 00:21:31.240
The Doctor said that Newtypes can't emerge in a natural environment!

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:36.370
Someone created your powers just like they created mine, right?

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.920
No! Mine are different!

00:21:40.340 --> 00:21:45.340
But then... Are you saying that you were born with your abilities?

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.690
That's quite far enough.

00:22:05.190 --> 00:22:07.360
Both Gundams are completely pinned down!

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:10.570
I wonder if Garrod is okay...

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.240
Orders, Captain?

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:18.670
You've learned too much.

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:20.540
What are you gonna do about it?

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:24.840
I'm going to do this.

00:22:24.920 --> 00:22:25.960
Garrod!

00:22:26.670 --> 00:22:30.640
It's too late for regrets. This is what you get for spurning me.

00:22:45.650 --> 00:22:50.950
<b>Can I find the words to tell you</b>

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.570
Carris has learned the truth.

00:22:50.660 --> 00:22:57.290
Tiffa, whom he had believed to be like him, was something else entirely.

00:22:50.950 --> 00:22:56.330
<b>How I live between the walls of steel and stone</b>

00:22:57.620 --> 00:23:00.710
This shock leads him to regret his bloody past.

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:04.170
<b>How I close my eyes to find some kind of rapture</b>

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:06.740
Carris challenges Garrod in battle in order to atone for his actions.

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:10.510
<b>In a world where you can feel so all alone</b>

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:17.520
<b>Inside I'm full of light and laughter</b>

00:23:18.980 --> 00:23:21.390
<b>There's a flame that burns in me</b>

00:23:21.390 --> 00:23:22.350
<b>(I need a way)</b>

00:23:22.350 --> 00:23:26.440
<b>(I need a way) I need a way to set it free</b>

00:23:26.440 --> 00:23:31.360
<b>When you find love in your heart</b>

00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:33.490
<b>(The human touch)</b>

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:37.540
<b>You can believe from the start</b>

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:39.540
<b>(From the start)</b>

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:42.670
<b>Dreams they come true</b>

00:23:42.670 --> 00:23:44.040
<b>(They come true)</b>

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:48.380
<b>All comes to you, oh all at once</b>

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:50.800
Shoot me for being a fool.

00:23:48.380 --> 00:23:52.180
<b>If you believe in human touch</b>

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:56.430
<b>Episode 13</b>

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:56.430
<b>"Shoot Me For Being a Fool"</b>

00:23:56.430 --> 00:23:58.430
<b></b>
